 - Bash: git log --follow --format='%h %ad %an <%ae> | %s' --date=short -- lib/index.js | head -80; echo; git log --follow --format='%an' -- lib/index.js | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20; wc -l lib/index.js
 - Bash: git show --stat --format='%h %an <%ae>%ncommitter: %cn <%ce> %cd%n%B' b2005d9 62628c0; git show b2005d9 -- lib/index.js | head -80; echo ---NAIVE; git blame --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; echo ---IGNORE-REFORMAT; git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; ls .git-blame-ignore-revs 2>/dev/null
 - Bash: git blame -w -M -C --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9 --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author-mail ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; echo; git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9 lib/index.js | awk '{print $1}' | grep -c '^\*\|^0000'; git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9 --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^summary ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -25; git diff b2005d9 62628c0 -w --stat -- lib/index.js
FINAL ANSWER:
`lib/index.js` was largely written by Troy Goode, the project's creator, and his code is still most of the file. A plain `git blame` gives the wrong answer, though: it credits "Fiona Formatter" with 214 of the 238 lines. That's because of two recent commits that changed no logic, so I ran blame again with both of them ignored.

## The two recent commits that skew blame

- **`62628c0` (2026-04-12), Fiona Formatter:** "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes". It's purely cosmetic: it touched every line of `lib/index.js` (plus the test files) to change indentation and quote style.
- **`b2005d9` (2026-04-10), "Troy Goode <troy@laptop.example>":** "lib: annotate handlers". It only adds `// checked` comments to the ends of 12 function signature lines. Note that the email is `troy@laptop.example`, not the `<email redacted>` address on every one of Troy's other commits since 2013. Git can't confirm it's the same person, so I've counted it separately and left it out of his totals.

## How the file developed (66 commits, 2013–2026)

1. **2013–2014, Troy Goode writes the core.** His "first commit" was on 2013-01-30. After that came case-insensitive header lookup, `origin: false`, and the big restructure "wrapping up" (Oct 2013). In 2014 he added Express 4 support and switched to the `vary` module (#30/#33). Contributors in this period included:
   - Simon Mansfield: early origin checks and where the credentials header goes
   - Eric di Domenico: `origin` as a callback
   - Mathias Buus: support for apps that don't use Express
   - Typicode: added PATCH to the default methods
   - Shane Tomlinson: uppercase method names
   - Igor Soarez: `Vary: Origin`
2. **2015, community features.**
   - Raymond Feng: made `applyHeaders` faster
   - Alejandro Caravaca Puchades: RegExp and array `origin` matching (5 commits)
   - max.laverse: `preflightContinue`
   - DracoBlue: exposed headers on OPTIONS
   - Troy's switch to ESLint and cleanup (#42)
3. **2016–2018, Douglas Christopher Wilson maintains it** (the Express/jshttp maintainer). He handled `Vary` correctness, the missing-`methods` fix and the lint/eslint updates. Others in this period:
   - Saad Tazi: fix for frozen options
   - Tomek Kopczuk: `Vary` with regex origins
   - Benjamin Eidelman: Safari pre-flight workaround
   - Tom Arad: `maxAge: 0`
4. **2021:** LuisEGR removed unused parameters.
5. **2026:** the two cosmetic commits above.

By number of commits that touched the file, Troy has 29, Wilson 4, Caravaca Puchades 5 (counting both his name spellings), Mansfield 3 and jordandenison 2. Everyone else has one each.

## Whose code is in it today

These counts come from `git blame -w -M -C --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9`:

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 157 | ~66% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | ~9% |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 16 | ~7% |
| Raymond Feng | 9 | ~4% |
| max.laverse | 6 | |
