| Chima Alaebo, Tom Arad, Shane Tomlinson, Eran Tiktin, Hannah Wolfe | 1 each | |

The commits with the most surviving lines are Troy's "wrapping up" (58 lines, 2013) and "#42: now passing all tests again" (34). After those come "support Access-Control-Expose-Headers" (19) and Wilson's dynamic-`allowedHeaders` `Vary` fix (17).

A few contributors from the log have no lines left, because their code has since been rewritten: DracoBlue, Tomek Kopczuk, jordandenison and Typicode.

One caveat: even with whitespace ignored, the reformat still changes 32 lines because of the switch to double quotes. `--ignore-rev` passes those lines back to earlier authors using git's heuristics, so a few line counts could be off by one or two. The overall picture is solid.

To make GitHub and local blame skip the reformat automatically, you could add `62628c0` to a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file (the repo doesn't have one yet) and run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`.

